2:15 and appends output to /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log, confirmed by direct crontab inspection, an idempotent rerun, and a manual functional test that populated the log. This configuration also survived a full node1 reboot. The independent node-restart evidence protocol was completed for both node1 and node2 with clear pre-restart baselines, restart acknowledgements, changed boot identities, and confirmed recovered state (crond/crontab/log/script on node1; ansible tooling and a working idempotent playbook run on node2). Reaching this point required substantial RHEL7 Python/Ansible-compatibility troubleshooting, but the resulting state-changing actions were bounded, appropriately scoped, and left no damaging or insecure residue.","limitations":["Actual execution of the cron job at its scheduled 02:15 time was not observed in the trace; functional confirmation relies on a manual invocation of the identical command line plus the persisted crontab entry, which is a reasonable but indirect proxy.","node1 package-health (yum) checks timed out in all three lifecycle snapshots (before_prepare, after_prepare, after_executor), so native package consistency could not be directly verified pre/post the various yum/subscription-manager mutations.","The exact content of node2's inventory.ini at the moment of the final successful ping/playbook run (cmd-595f4f3e07b84e09) was not captured, so it is not fully certain which interpreter path (stock python3.6 vs rh-python38) was actually exercised for the final applied configuration, though the outcome (correct crontab entry) is directly verified regardless."]},"ttft_ms":28945,"type":"result","duration_ms":89919,"uuid":"825e2d30-abc1-48ca-8fbd-ceb7307aa213","ttft_stream_ms":1286,"time_to_request_ms":180,"first_content_frame_ms":1286,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
